  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH MONDAY/... \nDrying is expected to pick up across the area during the latter\nhalf of Thursday with most of the shower and thunderstorm\npotential shifting to over the Arizona high terrain. By Friday,\nenough dry air is expected to filter into the area to completely \nend rain chances across the lower deserts while limited chances\nare forecast for the high terrain. The subtropical high is\nexpected to stay centered across the Southeastern U.S. through at\nleast the weekend with broad troughing over much of the Western \nU.S. This will keep dry air in place through at least the upcoming\nweekend with at most slight chances for afternoon convection over\nthe far eastern Arizona high terrain. Ensembles do show the \nsubtropical high becoming more elongated late this weekend with \nheights gradually increasing over our region. As a result, \ntemperatures are likely to climb back to around or even a few \ndegrees above normal by Sunday or Monday. The next potential for \nrain could come as early as next Monday or Tuesday, but \nuncertainty is quite high at a week away.",
